---
title: "Running Embedded In-Process Qdrant with FastEmbed"
description: "How to run local, zero-infrastructure vector search with embedded Qdrant and FastEmbed ONNX models in Python and Node.js."
sidebar:
  order: 6
---

This page is superseded by the [Edge runtime](/docs/edge/). Edge is the
canonical reference for in-process QQL with local HNSW storage and optional
local ONNX embeddings.

Start with [Getting started](/docs/edge/getting-started/) for the end to end
local session, then see [Embedding models](/docs/edge/models/) for model
slots and [Capabilities](/docs/edge/capabilities/) for the exact offline
boundary and error codes.

Python uses the `pyqql-edge` package and Node.js uses
`@veristamp/nqql-edge`. Both expose the same declarative QQL dialect as
remote Qdrant backends, with no server and no network at inference time.
